course: dictionary
lesson: 4686
title: Homemade and what it tells us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Homemade is made of two words, home and made. It means made at home, not bought from a shop or factory. «Galileo's homemade telescope» was made by Galileo himself, so it was not bought in a shop.
explain: Homemade things often show care and effort. «A small or homemade present is fine» means the present does not have to be expensive or bought. The person made it by hand, so the thought behind it counts most.
explain: Look at the words around homemade. «Amara brings shop biscuits to the cake sale... they help just as much as homemade cupcakes.» Shop biscuits are bought and homemade cupcakes are made in a kitchen, so homemade is the opposite of shop-bought.
fact: Homemade means made at home, not bought from a shop or factory.
fact: «Homemade cake», «homemade soup», «homemade card» and «homemade costume» are all things someone made by hand.
fact: In 1609-1610, Galileo used a small «homemade telescope» to discover four moons of Jupiter.
fact: In the 1670s, Antonie van Leeuwenhoek used «homemade lenses» to see tiny living things in water.
fact: Never try to make fireworks or chemicals at home: homemade ones are very dangerous.
exercise: What does homemade mean? | Bought from a big shop in town | Made by a machine in a factory | *Made at home, not bought from a shop or factory | Very old and rare
exercise: In «shop biscuits... homemade cupcakes», what is the opposite of homemade? | Glowing | Ancient | Giant | *Shop-bought
exercise: Which of these is a homemade present? | A box of sweets from a supermarket | A gift card from the shop | A toy bought from a big shop | *A card you drew and made at the kitchen table
test: Galileo used a «small homemade telescope». Why is it called homemade? | It was a famous telescope from a city shop | A factory machine built it | He found it on a beach | *He made it himself, at home
test: Which thing is very dangerous and should never be tried at home? | Baking a homemade cake with an adult | *Making homemade fireworks | Making a homemade card for a friend | Sewing a homemade costume for a play
exam: Which sentence uses homemade correctly? | *Mum made homemade soup for tea | The shop sold homemade television sets | The homemade bus took us to school | The factory made homemade cars all day
